Procedure
Step 1: Launch Windows EC2 Instance
Open AWS Console.
Go to EC2 → Launch Instance.
Select Windows Server AMI.
Choose instance type.
Create/select key pair.
Configure Security Group:
Allow RDP
Port 3389
Source My IP
Launch instance.
Step 2: Obtain Public IP/DNS
Go to EC2 → Instances.
Select Windows instance.
Copy Public IP or DNS.
Step 3: Retrieve Administrator Password
Select instance.
Click:
Connect → RDP Client
Click Get Password.
Upload .pem file.
Click Decrypt Password.
Copy generated Administrator password.
Step 4: Connect Using Remote Desktop
Open Remote Desktop Connection (mstsc).
Enter Public IP/DNS.
Click Connect.
Login using:
Username: Administrator
Password: decrypted password
Step 5: Verify Connection
Windows desktop appears.
Use instance like normal Windows system.
Observation
Windows EC2 instance launched successfully.
RDP port 3389 enabled.
Administrator password decrypted using key pair.
Remote Desktop connection established successfully.
Result

Successfully created a Windows EC2 instance and connected securely using Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP).
